    "summary": "Shawm [algaita], (a) made of wood covered with leather for three-quarters of length. Three fingerholes along centre of shawm and one double hole at top of shawm. Leather carrying strap attached to instrument at junction between wood and leather-covered sections. Mouthpiece (b) made of hollow metal tube bound with cotton thread at lower end terminating in a reed, made of cane, bound with cotton thread, below which is sheet metal disc.",
